            },
            {
                "entry_id": "ab61fe6c-e428-3ed1-8032-82682f52a636",
                "word": "tatterdemalion",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "120ce3cd-e231-4d22-b94f-72d60765b5d3",
                        "entry_id": "ab61fe6c-e428-3ed1-8032-82682f52a636",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "tatterdemalions"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                        "entry_id": "ab61fe6c-e428-3ed1-8032-82682f52a636",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person with tattered clothing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "691cd8d7-28c7-4213-b42b-d00fa8cc88ba",
                                "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                                "text": "[…] we haue ordeined that through euery ward […] there be erected one sound, sufficient, and well painted whipping poste, the very sight of which wil not only scarre them, worse then the scowting face of a Serieant being seen peeping through a red lettice, frights a yong gallant, but also in time driue the whole band of Tatterdemalions from poste to piller."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14eca642-2e7e-444e-880f-7dc9df4c9ecb",
                                "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                                "text": "St. Martin [of Tours] looks round, first, deliberately;—becomes aware of a tatterdemalion and thirsty-looking soul of a beggar at his chair side, who has managed to get his cup filled somehow, also—by a charitable lacquey. St. Martin turns his back on the Empress, and hobnobs with him!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de12b956-a6c8-4cd5-a680-20f963e180f8",
                                "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                                "text": "She took romantic fancies to vagabonds of either sex, attempted to establish social relations with them, and was the cause of infinite agitation to the gentleman who lived near her in the Crescent, who was always smoking at the window, and who reminded Hyacinth of Mr. Micawber. She received visits that were a scandal to the Crescent, and Hyacinth neglected his affairs, whatever they were, to see what tatterdemalion would next turn up at her door."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab08cb95-46b1-4939-8488-a897741d6b20",
                                "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                                "text": "Rags mounted guard over the treasure. Virtue rendered these tatterdemalions resplendent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c1462e8-190f-4716-a418-ed61d9740e95",
                                "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                                "text": "[…] we found hundreds of Cuban insurgents, a crew of as utter tatterdemalions as human eyes ever looked on, armed with every kind of rifle in all stages of dilapidation. It was evident, at a glance, that they would be no use in serious fighting."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f77d385a-5cf6-41c3-a96e-dbc1fb4a2672",
                                "sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                                "text": "Whenever his name was mentioned, she had a vague impression of a bearded tatterdemalion like Ben Gunn in Treasure Island, leading a lonely existence on some bleak, salty islet, his pants in rags and his wristwatch corroded from the seawater."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "55ccf423-af69-4fc5-817d-ff009e0667a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab61fe6c-e428-3ed1-8032-82682f52a636",
                        "source_sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                        "source_sense_description": "person with tattered clothing",
                        "target_lang_word": "trhan",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trhan",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4a1e5bb5-9b24-36c0-94ae-29f87ffeaaa7",
                                        "entry_id": "9cacd43c-3d74-3517-b39e-fc65bd1e1b55",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "člověk, který nosí často nebo pořád zanedbané, roztrhané oblečení"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a3ed79fd-e2a9-4871-a7d0-31519d1fd2e6",
                        "source_entry_id": "ab61fe6c-e428-3ed1-8032-82682f52a636",
                        "source_sense_id": "3914d8b5-f506-3506-8f18-d1a08226c063",
                        "source_sense_description": "person with tattered clothing",
                        "target_lang_word": "loqueteux",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "loqueteux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e34d6e03-789f-37b9-94e6-c5e69c111bfd",
                                        "entry_id": "604c3c43-3a11-36a9-acff-6e062d244f18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est en loques, en parlant des vêtements."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd9aef8e-0cd0-4cf4-b3b0-627a4d678d80",
                                                "sense_id": "e34d6e03-789f-37b9-94e6-c5e69c111bfd",
                                                "text": "Sélem, l’aîné des deux frères, s’écarta de notre groupe et, étendant son burnous loqueteux sur le sable, il commença à prier, grave et comme grandi."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03723710-3bf9-31f7-bc0c-dfbfb173092b",
                                        "entry_id": "604c3c43-3a11-36a9-acff-6e062d244f18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui a des vêtements en loques"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e44553e1-2fd3-4594-b81d-2b0e2a5e9051",
                                                "sense_id": "03723710-3bf9-31f7-bc0c-dfbfb173092b",
                                                "text": "Et bientôt, au milieu d’une foule grouillante où toutes les races se mêlent, assailli par une nuée de gamins loqueteux qui parlent « parisien », l’on débarque sur ce coin de terre chérifienne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f54810-1bdc-43df-93cd-ca95f90937e9",
                                                "sense_id": "03723710-3bf9-31f7-bc0c-dfbfb173092b",
                                                "text": "Des garnis sans rideaux, des gargotes, des débits grouillants de vermine occupent — entre les loges des filles — la longueur des façades et une humanité malpropre, hébétée, loqueteuse s'y agite machinalement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7524075-53b9-4fed-8882-5c89e30882a5",
                                                "sense_id": "03723710-3bf9-31f7-bc0c-dfbfb173092b",
                                                "text": "Le serki de Sissy, grand vieillard maigre et loqueteux, arrive essoufflé. Il se déchausse pour m’aborder, esquisse un salut militaire et s’accroupit à l'entrée de ma paillote."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "loqueteux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cae5e812-76e5-3072-8f7a-29681837f0fd",
                                        "entry_id": "ef66d0da-6efb-3ba1-8a11-4b8193885383",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne dont les vêtements sont en loques."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "309999da-29b7-46a6-b587-e52ee6eba3e9",
                                                "sense_id": "cae5e812-76e5-3072-8f7a-29681837f0fd",
                                                "text": "Une douzaine de loqueteux se pressent en rond autour dun gros tas de flammèches grésillantes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d70b796e-3c84-3fb6-bc79-112a44c718a9",
                                        "entry_id": "ef66d0da-6efb-3ba1-8a11-4b8193885383",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gueux, misérable"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "familiar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "119066b1-5f6c-4bdf-971e-c68035e8a767",
                                                "sense_id": "d70b796e-3c84-3fb6-bc79-112a44c718a9",
                                                "text": "Par bonheur, on arrivait dans un village dont j’ai oublié le nom, village, il est vrai, rempli déjà d’un nombre infini de loqueteux et de claquedents."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56d204c8-54d3-4280-a096-ba1afb660f15",
                                                "sense_id": "d70b796e-3c84-3fb6-bc79-112a44c718a9",
                                                "text": "Mais l’agent veille, l’agent-planton payé supplémentairement, nourri, abreuvé par le restaurant : il saute sur les loqueteux en donnant de la voix, débarrasse le trottoir, dégage la chaussée, et tout fier d’avoir préparé le chemin de l’Amour qui descend — parfois en titubant — l’escalier des salons, impressionné par le luxe des clients, par les perles des femmes, par les habits des hommes, il salue au passage, militairement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53600d8b-49f2-41e2-bd8b-2feb1ebca2ed",
                                                "sense_id": "d70b796e-3c84-3fb6-bc79-112a44c718a9",
                                                "text": "C'est un gadouilleux, un loqueteux, un panouilleux comme toi… Je sais, tu appelles ça « un homme libre ». Et pourquoi pas, après tout ? Si je le garde avec moi, ça fera un blouson doré, peut-être une petite crapule."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
